Nothing is vendored. What was taken is design, re-implemented against this
project's own shapes, and each borrow site names its original in a comment:

  eval/harness.py   percentile() / latency()
                    Reporting shape from scripts/iso-certify.py: count, p50, p95,
                    p99 and max returned together, so no percentile is ever
                    printed without the sample size that produced it. The
                    arithmetic itself is statistics.quantiles(method="inclusive"),
                    which is Python's standard library.

